Well, I went out to altair to check out your sheet thing.  I fetched
nh_a4.ps, just to see what it was.  Naturally, looking at the postscript
file directly was absolutely meaningless.

And so I went to print it out on the local laser printer.  For the
most part it looks okay, but I've got a couple problems/questions.

It seems your design is slightly bigger than 8-1/2 by 11 inches.
I miss the leftmost 2-3 columns, which fall under 'Neth' on the
left side of the page.  Does this mean I'm supposed to use
'nh_let.ps'?  I didn't get any impression from the commentary that
the different forms implied different sizes of paper.

From the half the page that I do see clearly: I notice that
M1-M10 and Q1-Q7 are all listed.  From my experience with those
areas, I don't find that all of those levels are interesting.
Knowing which is the Town, and where the bottoms are will usually
suffice.  Aside from that, maybe we'd only care if something
had a ghost pile.

If I'm extrapolating what I don't see correctly, it might be possible
to just use the left side of the sheet to record any Mine or Quest
levels which have special stuff.  Clearing out the big box on the
right might allow for a reorganization of the sheet (as I will
show below).  I'd try it myself, but I am completely postscript
illiterate:

Nethack 3.1 Dungeon Info Sheet 1.1         Branches                  Actual
Lev Sp Sh Al Te Fo Sk Tr Vt Pi Remarks     G  the Gnomish Mines D2-5  ___
                                           Q  the Quest, DO+(6-8)     ___
"Everything as before"                     L  Fort Ludios, D18-22     ___

include Mine/Quest levels with             Specials
ghost hordes here.                         O  the Oracle, D5-10       ___
                                           B  the BIg Room D10-D13    ___
                                              etc.
Legend for [Lev,Sp,Fo, etc] goes on either
side (left or right) as space permits.


I see a couple advantages to this approach:
The right side of this will be relatively narrow, allowing more
room for remarks on the left side.  Also, everything can fit
nicely inside of 11 inches.

Also, just having the notations on the side which indicate where
the special levels and branches are means that you might not even
need to mark down a level just because it is Special.

For example, I've never seen a Big Room, Oracle, or Rogue Level
that had a Vault, a Shop, or a Throne Room.  This would mean that
a level might be annotated on the left side of the sheet only
if it had an Altar/Temple/Sink/Fountain, etc.

I'd like to know what you think...  I'd hate to throw more work
at you just because I'm Postscript illiterate, but this does seem
like a cool idea.

I only have to consistently play more games which get far enough
for me to take advantage of this.  :)

Roger Christman


